sponded, leaning toward A but wants D discussion.\n\nNow as Agent 3, we need to make a focused argumentative contribution, referencing discussion, using explicit facts, and state current recommendation. We need to decide vote. Let's evaluate.\n\nWe have candidate facts:\n\nA: quick correct decisions, excellent attention, puts concern for others above everything, creates positive atmosphere, 100% reliable, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, calm in crisis.\n\nB: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, grumpy, uncooperative, sometimes adopts wrong tone, pretentious.\n\nC: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, unfriendly, eats unhealthily, can be unorganized, not good at taking criticism.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, moody, loner, hot temper, know-it-all.\n\nNow we need to weigh criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility, adaptability, etc.\n\nA: reliability high (100% reliable), decision speed, calm in crisis, attention, concern for others. Weakness: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Cooperation? He puts concern for others above everything, creates positive atmosphere, but communication issues may hinder crew cooperation. Still, his concern for others suggests potential for cooperation if communication improved.\n\nB: reliability (very conscientious), stress resilience (handles stress well), technical competence (weather, computer), but cooperation issues (grumpy, uncooperative, wrong tone, pretentious). Communication issues but maybe less severe than A's difficulty communicating ideas? Both have issues.\n\nC: technical competence high (anticipate danger, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership), but cooperation issues (unfriendly, not good at criticism, unorganized, unhealthy). Stress resilience unknown. Health may affect long flights.\n\nD: problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but cooperation issues (loner, moody, hot temper, know-it-all). Stress resilience unknown.\n\nThus likely best candidate is either A or B. Need to decide based on evidence. A has strong reliability, decision making, calm, attention, concern for others. Communication issues are serious but maybe can be trained. B has stress resilience and technical competence, but cooperation issues also serious. Which is more critical? For long-distance pilot, crew cooperation and communication are vital. A's egocentric and difficulty communicating may be more severe than B's grumpy/uncooperative? Both are concerning. However, A's willingness to prioritize others suggests potential for cooperation if communication improved. B's uncooperative and pretentious may be more ingrained.\n\nThus I might lean toward Candidate A as leading, as Agent 1 suggested. But we need to consider D's problem solving and responsibility. D's interpersonal issues are significant.\n\nThus I will state my recommendation: Candidate A, with note that communication training needed, but overall best fit.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: agree with Agent 1's leaning toward A, but also note that D's strengths not enough to outweigh his interpersonal deficits. Also compare with B: B's stress resilience is good but his cooperation issues are more severe. Provide evidence: B is \"grumpy\", \"uncooperative\", \"pretentious\". A's concern for others and positive atmosphere offset his communication gaps.\n\nThus vote for Candidate A.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
